  "id": "modality",
  "term": "modality",
  "definition": "Modality is the logical way a statement or fact is qualified by such modes as possible, impossible, necessary, or contingent. In this historical sense, it concerns whether something is presented as required, allowed, excluded, or dependent on circumstances.",
